    "done_when": "reckon/worker_git_shim.py reads `git worktree list` as a read form whatever output options it carries, so --porcelain, -z, -v and --expired, alone or together, are admitted for any repository while RECKON_RUN_ID is set. Every mutating worktree action (add, remove, move, prune, lock, unlock, repair) stays refused outside the run's own worktree and scratch repositories. tests/test_git_shim_checks_the_resolved_repo.py gains cases, each run in a child process group under a 60 s timeout with two shim directories on PATH. 1: git worktree list --porcelain, run with -C pointing at a synthesised foreign checkout, succeeds with RECKON_RUN_ID set and prints that checkout's worktree. 2: git worktree prune, run with -C pointing at the same checkout, is still refused and its worktree metadata is unchanged. 3: reckon.crew.routing._registered_worktrees, called with RECKON_RUN_ID set against a synthesised repository, returns its worktrees rather than raising. A declared negative control is executed and logged under pytest: restoring the list-only read option turns cases 1 and 3 red. The node gate is that test file at head, ending EXIT=0. Every log sits under the run directory, headed with revision, tree and literal command, and ends EXIT=. Only reckon/worker_git_shim.py and tests/test_git_shim_checks_the_resolved_repo.py change.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
